From 253b1c9dfe48d4f84c2bf672fcfcdb402f207013 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pablo Lopez <plopez@unc.edu.ar>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:41:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Read SWIFT (and Gadget-4 with gas) HDF5 snapshots with
 --input 105

- HDF5 header: read the attributes into vectors of the right size, so
  snapshots with 7 particle types (SWIFT) and a 3D BoxSize no longer write
  past the end of the header structure; types >= 6 are ignored with a
  warning; cosmological parameters are also read from /Parameters
  (Gadget-4) and /Cosmology (SWIFT).
- Particle masses: read the 'Masses' dataset (Gadget-4, SWIFT) or 'Mass'
  (Gadget-2/3).
- Help text and README: input formats (there is no '--input 102'),
  SWIFT notes and the interpolation bug fix.

Tested with snapshots that reproduce the SWIFT layout (gas + DM, float64
coordinates, per-particle masses, 7 types, 3D BoxSize, /Cosmology) in one
file, two files (%i) and a virtual file: identical density and velocity
to the same particles in the binary format 121.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C44ZCErHKsQgk681XW3FMn
---
 README.md                    |   3 +-
 src/io/gadget_reader_HDF5.cc | 183 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------
 src/user_options.cc          |   2 +-
 3 files changed, 131 insertions(+), 57 deletions(-)

